From: jamie@netcom.com (Jamie Dinkelacker)
Date: Sun, 23 Jan 1994 20:04:49 -0800
Subject: [#94-1-452] GOAL:  Reduce Sleep time

Regarding sleep. Who knows if this will work for anybody else, but here's
what works for me -- I sleep about 5 hours nightly. After years of
experimentation, here's what I've learned regarding myself -- the key: ease
of falling asleep leads to short, restful sleep. Here's what works for me:

(1) Peace of mind -- let the anger and frustration go, learn mental tricks
to get the "race of words" out of the mind prior to drifing off.
Personally, I replay favorite music in my head, stuff like Satie or other
largo movements.

(2) Learn to relax -- meditation helps, but anything that leads to removing
bodily tension. Be especially aware of tension in the tongue and jaw,
forehead and eyes. This includes learning how to sit still with contantly
jiggling feet or fingers. Choose to have a positive attitude.

(3) Minimize the amount of blood meat ingested -- e.g., I only eat beef in
restaurants when it's part of a dish served "family style." No pork, lamb,
venison or other "red" meat. Avoid fried foods.

(4) Minimize salt intake, eat a well-balanced diet with loads of fruits and
veggies.

(5) Drink lots of water, minimize alcohol, avoid smokey places.

(6) Regular exercise; watch weight.

(7) Keep records on food/life/stuff so subtle patterns can be detected and
incorporated or rejected from daily living.

This works for me; who knows if it has benefit to anyone else.

BTW: I was raised in the land of Rip Van Winkle!


