>My interest in sleep reduction occurred long after I got into nutrients.  I 
>sleep about 8 hours per night, but tended to sleep more in my youth.  I 
>always attributed this to going to school and later getting a job!  Maybe 
>my sleep has reduced since taking suppliments, but I'm not really sure.

I recall reading somewhere about the importance of ``sleep cycles''.
According to this theory, your sleep is not a uniform thing, and it seems
to follow cycles of a certain duration.

What is interesting about his theory is: you tend to be more productive
if your start/end your sleep in accordance with the begining/end of the sleep
cycles. Once the process of tunign to your natural sleep cycles is achieved,
one can then slowly and regularly ``squeeze'' the cycle, and thus gain time.

If anybody's got infos about, directions to, references to this theory, I'd
be glad if they could send some.

